  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 5af86c06a1cd5294e909c2ee75d2c673, type: 3}
  m_Name: HisaTeacherNPCDialogue
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::NPCDialogue
  npcName: Halyna
  npcPortrait: {fileID: -6471082416391893753, guid: 53d5f5efd048d2d4081b29c56deb11a6, type: 3}
  dialogueLines:
  - Oh! You surprised me.
  - People rarely come to this street.
  - "Well\u2026 Let me see. That is this house."
  - A Jewish family. Long before my time.
  - My grandmother talked about them sometimes.
  - A big family. The house was never quiet.
  - They never came back after the war.
  - "After that\u2026 the authorities let us move in. "
  - We were five children. One room each felt like a miracle.
  - Every Friday they walked to the market where she worked.
  - All dressed up.  Like it was a holiday.
  - "Ah\u2026 that. The old owners had something there. "
  - A small little case.
  - My father once tried to sand it away. Said it looked strange.
  - But the mark never disappeared.
  - "Anyway\u2026 I was just about to go out."
  - My friend turned seventy today. Imagine that!
  - I promised her a bouquet.
  - These days I prefer flowers to cake. Easier on the teeth.
  - Wildflowers grow around the street.
  - Would you help me gather a few?
  - Well...
  - While you do that, I'll see if I can find something inside.
  - Your photograph reminded me of it.
  - Flowers from the street smell better than the ones from shops.
  - Oh! You actually did it. Beautiful! She'll love these.
  - 'And look what I found. A small wooden box. '
  - The only thing that stayed here from the previous family.
  - My parents opened it once, many years ago.
  - Some old postcards inside. Maybe letters too.
  - "But the key\u2026 That is the problem."
  - My husband had a box full of little things.
  - "Keys, coins\u2026 You know how it goes."
  - If the key survived, it will be in that box.
  - "Well\u2026  Look at that. After all these years."
  - "Maybe\u2026  this was waiting for you."
